{"notebook":"nb1","page":3,"seed":3,"says":"I will take half of that. Sharpening between tones is simply how a shaded study is done, so the mug gets a fresh point for its outline, its steam, its body and its lettering, and I will not pretend that is thrift. The big erasure I like too: I am blacking in the wall behind the cup and then rubbing the steam out of it, and drawing the curls into the cleaned paper. What I refuse is filling the mullions and margins just because they are empty. White paper is where the light comes from. The mug's bright side stays bare.","before":{"length":169.65105525188673,"worn":0.05320405916709766,"eraser":11.980383005217794,"sharpenings":1,"graphite":3.375738222613676,"distance":51694.89419122923},"after":{"length":162.43474008757852,"worn":0.023130241946342018,"eraser":11.907620789041108,"sharpenings":4,"graphite":5.066142484611321,"distance":83727.36444284153},"stats":{"strokeM":32.03247025160834,"graphite":1.6904042619976634,"used":7.216315164308213,"sharpenings":3,"erasedMm2":440,"coverage":0.07439321202690537,"stopped":false},"warnings":[],"ops":[{"op":"write","text":"7:15. Coffee.","x":14,"y":22,"size":7},{"op":"ellipse","cx":74,"cy":92,"rx":26,"ry":7,"pressure":1},{"op":"ellipse","cx":74,"cy":92.8,"rx":23.5,"ry":5.6,"pressure":0.8},{"op":"line","x1":48,"y1":92,"x2":50,"y2":138},{"op":"line","x1":100,"y1":92,"x2":98,"y2":138},{"op":"curve","points":[[50,138],[51.17,140.01],[54.58,141.82],[59.89,143.26],[66.58,144.18],[74,144.5],[81.42,144.18],[88.11,143.26],[93.42,141.82],[96.83,140.01],[98,138]]},{"op":"curve","points":[[101.57,102.11],[104.19,102.8],[106.63,104.1],[108.79,105.95],[110.57,108.27],[111.9,110.96],[112.72,113.92],[113,117],[112.72,120.08],[111.9,123.04],[110.57,125.73],[108.79,128.05],[106.63,129.9],[104.19,131.2],[101.57,131.89]],"pressure":1},{"op":"curve","points":[[101.53,108.22],[103.02,108.88],[104.35,109.95],[105.46,111.38],[106.3,113.09],[106.82,114.99],[107,117],[106.82,119.01],[106.3,120.91],[105.46,122.62]